{"title":"Career roadmap · Audit Associate","role":"Audit Associate","summary":"Career alignment:\nB.Com in Accounting & Finance is a strong undergraduate route for an Audit Associate. The student should develop expertise in financial accounting, auditing, taxation basics, internal controls, Excel, audit documentation, financial statement analysis and professional standards.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An important distinction is that an Audit Associate is not automatically a Chartered Accountant. The role can be entered through accounting/audit firms with a B.Com, while becoming a CA is a separate professional qualification pathway."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Typical roles"],"rows":[[{"text":"0–1 year"},{"text":"Audit Intern, Audit Associate, Accounts Associate"}],[{"text":"1–3 years"},{"text":"Audit Associate, Senior Audit Associate"}],[{"text":"3–5 years"},{"text":"Audit Senior, Audit Supervisor"}],[{"text":"5–8 years"},{"text":"Audit Manager, Assistant Manager"}],[{"text":"8+ years"},{"text":"Senior Manager, Director, Partner / Head of Internal Audit"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"Possible work environments:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Audit firms"},{"text":"Accounting firms"},{"text":"Consulting firms"},{"text":"Internal audit departments"},{"text":"Banks and financial institutions"},{"text":"Corporate finance teams"},{"text":"Shared-service/GCC finance centres"}]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During B.Com","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Accounting Foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Build a strong understanding of:"},{"type":"h","text":"Financial accounting"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Journal entries"},{"text":"Ledger"},{"text":"Trial balance"},{"text":"Bank reconciliation"},{"text":"Accruals"},{"text":"Prepayments"},{"text":"Depreciation"},{"text":"Provisions"},{"text":"Inventory"},{"text":"Receivables"},{"text":"Payables"},{"text":"Fixed assets"},{"text":"Revenue recognition"},{"text":"Financial statements"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand how:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Transactions","Ledger","Trial Balance","Adjustments","Financial Statements"]},{"type":"h","text":"Economics & business"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Microeconomics"},{"text":"Macroeconomics"},{"text":"Business mathematics"},{"text":"Business statistics"},{"text":"Corporate structure"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Tools"},{"type":"p","text":"Start with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Google Sheets"},{"text":"Accounting software"},{"text":"PowerPoint"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Projects"},{"type":"p","text":"Build:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Complete accounting cycle in Excel"},{"text":"Bank-reconciliation model"},{"text":"Financial-statement preparation project"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Auditing Fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"This is the most important stage for the target role."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"h","text":"Auditing concepts"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Audit objectives"},{"text":"Audit planning"},{"text":"Audit evidence"},{"text":"Audit risk"},{"text":"Materiality"},{"text":"Internal controls"},{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Substantive procedures"},{"text":"Analytical procedures"},{"text":"Audit documentation"},{"text":"Management assertions"},{"text":"Working papers"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Assertions"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Existence"},{"text":"Completeness"},{"text":"Accuracy"},{"text":"Cut-off"},{"text":"Valuation"},{"text":"Rights and obligations"},{"text":"Presentation/classification"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For example:"},{"type":"h","text":"Inventory"},{"type":"flow","items":["Does it exist?","Is it complete?","Is it correctly valued?","Is it recorded in the correct period?"]},{"type":"h","text":"Internal Controls"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand common control areas:"},{"type":"h","text":"Revenue"},{"type":"flow","items":["Customer order","Invoice","Delivery","Collection"]},{"type":"h","text":"Purchases"},{"type":"flow","items":["Purchase request","PO","Goods receipt","Invoice","Payment"]},{"type":"h","text":"Payroll"},{"type":"flow","items":["Employee master","Attendance","Payroll calculation","Approval","Payment"]},{"type":"h","text":"Cash"},{"type":"flow","items":["Receipt","Recording","Bank reconciliation","Review"]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn how to identify:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Control gaps"},{"text":"Segregation-of-duties issues"},{"text":"Authorisation failures"},{"text":"Duplicate payments"},{"text":"Unusual transactions"},{"text":"Missing documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Excel for Audit"},{"type":"p","text":"Excel is one of the most useful tools for junior audit roles."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"XLOOKUP"},{"text":"INDEX/MATCH"},{"text":"SUMIFS"},{"text":"COUNTIFS"},{"text":"IF/IFS"},{"text":"IFERROR"},{"text":"Pivot Tables"},{"text":"Conditional formatting"},{"text":"Data validation"},{"text":"Sorting/filtering"},{"text":"Duplicate detection"},{"text":"Date calculations"},{"text":"Reconciliation"},{"text":"Power Query"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Audit-oriented Excel projects"},{"type":"p","text":"Build:"},{"type":"h","text":"Bank reconciliation"},{"type":"h","text":"Accounts receivable ageing"},{"type":"h","text":"Accounts payable analysis"},{"type":"h","text":"Expense testing"},{"type":"h","text":"Duplicate invoice detection"},{"type":"h","text":"Revenue cut-off testing"},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Audit Execution + Tax"},{"type":"p","text":"Move toward practical audit work."},{"type":"h","text":"Audit procedures"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn how to perform/understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Vouching"},{"text":"Verification"},{"text":"Reconciliation"},{"text":"Confirmation"},{"text":"Inspection"},{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"Recalculation"},{"text":"Analytical review"},{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Test of controls"},{"text":"Substantive testing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Working papers"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn how audit evidence is documented:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Objective","Population","Sample","Procedure","Evidence","Finding","Conclusion"]},{"type":"h","text":"Taxation Fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"For an Indian career pathway, understand the basics of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Income tax"},{"text":"TDS"},{"text":"GST"},{"text":"Corporate taxation concepts"},{"text":"Tax deductions"},{"text":"Tax compliance"},{"text":"Tax audit concepts"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The exact rules, thresholds and rates change, so students should use current official tax/GST guidance when preparing for professional work."},{"type":"h","text":"Accounting Standards"},{"type":"p","text":"Build familiarity with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Ind AS"},{"text":"Indian Accounting Standards concepts"},{"text":"IFRS fundamentals"},{"text":"Revenue recognition"},{"text":"Leases"},{"text":"Financial instruments"},{"text":"Provisions"},{"text":"Property, plant and equipment"},{"text":"Inventory"},{"text":"Cash-flow reporting"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Do not attempt to memorise every standard initially. Learn how standards affect financial statements and audit procedures."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 4 — Professional Audit Readiness"},{"type":"p","text":"The final year should focus on:"},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced audit"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Risk-based auditing"},{"text":"Financial statement audit"},{"text":"Internal audit"},{"text":"Internal control testing"},{"text":"Fraud-risk awareness"},{"text":"Data analytics"},{"text":"Audit sampling"},{"text":"Audit reporting"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technology"},{"type":"p","text":"Add:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"SQL basics"},{"text":"Power Query"},{"text":"Accounting/ERP systems"},{"text":"Audit analytics"},{"text":"Basic Python automation — optional"}]},{"type":"h","text":"ERP exposure"},{"type":"p","text":"Become familiar with concepts used in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SAP"},{"text":"Oracle"},{"text":"Microsoft Dynamics"},{"text":"Other ERP/accounting systems"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The goal is not to become an ERP consultant, but to understand how transactions flow through enterprise systems."},{"type":"h","text":"Final-Year Project"},{"type":"p","text":"Build an Audit Analytics & Financial Control Review System."},{"type":"h","text":"Example"},{"type":"h","text":"Financial Statement Audit Simulation"},{"type":"p","text":"Include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Trial balance"},{"text":"General ledger"},{"text":"Revenue transactions"},{"text":"Purchase transactions"},{"text":"Payroll data"},{"text":"Bank transactions"},{"text":"Accounts receivable"},{"text":"Accounts payable"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Then perform:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Duplicate transaction detection"},{"text":"Unusual journal-entry analysis"},{"text":"Revenue cut-off testing"},{"text":"Bank reconciliation"},{"text":"Receivables ageing"},{"text":"Expense analysis"},{"text":"Ratio analysis"},{"text":"Exception reporting"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Create a Power BI audit dashboard showing:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"High-risk transactions"},{"text":"Exception counts"},{"text":"Ageing"},{"text":"Revenue trends"},{"text":"Expense anomalies"},{"text":"Control issues"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This demonstrates practical audit thinking rather than just theoretical knowledge."},{"type":"h","text":"4-Year Honours / Advanced Variant"},{"type":"p","text":"If an honours/extended pathway is available, use the additional depth for:"},{"type":"h","text":"External Audit"},{"type":"flow","items":["Accounting","Audit","Financial Reporting","Risk","Assurance"]},{"type":"h","text":"Internal Audit"},{"type":"flow","items":["Internal Controls","Risk Assessment","Process Audit","Data Analytics"]},{"type":"h","text":"Tax Audit"},{"type":"flow","items":["Accounting","Taxation","GST","Income Tax","Tax Audit"]},{"type":"h","text":"Audit Analytics"},{"type":"flow","items":["Audit","Excel","Power Query","SQL","Power BI","Data Analytics"]},{"type":"h","text":"Specialisation Options"},{"type":"table","header":["Specialisation","Key skills"],"rows":[[{"text":"External Audit"},{"text":"Financial statements, audit procedures, reporting"}],[{"text":"Internal Audit"},{"text":"Controls, risk, process improvement"}],[{"text":"Tax Audit"},{"text":"Taxation, compliance, documentation"}],[{"text":"Forensic Audit"},{"text":"Fraud investigation, analytics, evidence"}],[{"text":"IT Audit"},{"text":"IT controls, cybersecurity, systems"}],[{"text":"Risk & Compliance"},{"text":"Risk assessment, controls, regulations"}],[{"text":"Audit Analytics"},{"text":"SQL, Excel, Power BI, data analytics"}],[{"text":"Financial Reporting"},{"text":"Accounting standards, reporting"}],[{"text":"ESG Assurance"},{"text":"Sustainability data, controls, assurance"}]]},{"type":"flow","items":["For this career target, Audit","Accounting","Excel","Internal Controls","Data Analytics is an especially useful combination."],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Level 1 — Accounting"},{"type":"flow","items":["Bookkeeping","Financial Statements","Accounting Standards"]},{"type":"h","text":"Level 2 — Audit"},{"type":"flow","items":["Assertions","Audit Risk","Evidence","Procedures"]},{"type":"h","text":"Level 3 — Controls"},{"type":"flow","items":["Internal Controls","Risk Assessment","Control Testing"]},{"type":"h","text":"Level 4 — Tools"},{"type":"flow","items":["Excel","Power Query","Accounting Software"]},{"type":"h","text":"Level 5 — Analytics"},{"type":"flow","items":["SQL","Power BI","Audit Analytics"]},{"type":"h","text":"Level 6 — Professional"},{"type":"flow","items":["Communication","Documentation","Professional Judgement"]},{"type":"h","text":"Level 7 — Specialisation"},{"type":"p","text":"Internal Audit / Tax / Forensics / IT Audit / Assurance"}]},{"heading":"Internships","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Start applying from Year 2."},{"type":"h","text":"Suitable internships"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Audit Intern"},{"text":"Accounts Intern"},{"text":"Internal Audit Intern"},{"text":"Tax Intern"},{"text":"Finance Intern"},{"text":"Assurance Intern"},{"text":"Risk & Compliance Intern"},{"text":"Audit Analytics Intern"}]},{"type":"h","text":"What to learn during an internship"},{"type":"p","text":"Try to get exposure to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Trial balance"},{"text":"General ledger"},{"text":"Financial statements"},{"text":"Vouching"},{"text":"Reconciliations"},{"text":"Audit working papers"},{"text":"Control testing"},{"text":"Accounts payable"},{"text":"Accounts receivable"},{"text":"Tax documentation"},{"text":"Client communication"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For audit, real working-paper and client-process exposure can be more valuable than collecting certificates."}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Professional Qualifications","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"CA — strongest professional route in India"},{"type":"p","text":"For students who want a long-term career in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Statutory audit"},{"text":"Assurance"},{"text":"Tax"},{"text":"Financial reporting"},{"text":"Practice"},{"text":"Audit leadership"}]},{"type":"p","text":"the CA pathway is highly relevant."},{"type":"p","text":"However:"},{"type":"h","text":"B.Com → Audit Associate"},{"type":"p","text":"does not require becoming a CA first."},{"type":"p","text":"CA is a separate professional qualification with its own current eligibility, examination and practical-training requirements. Students should verify the latest requirements directly with the Institute of Chartered Accountants of India."},{"type":"h","text":"Other options"},{"type":"h","text":"ACCA"},{"type":"p","text":"Useful for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"International accounting"},{"text":"Audit"},{"text":"Financial reporting"},{"text":"Global finance roles"}]},{"type":"h","text":"CMA"},{"type":"p","text":"Useful for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Management accounting"},{"text":"Cost management"},{"text":"FP&A"},{"text":"Corporate finance"}]},{"type":"h","text":"CIA"},{"type":"p","text":"Useful for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Internal audit"},{"text":"Risk"},{"text":"Internal controls"},{"text":"Governance"}]},{"type":"h","text":"CISA"},{"type":"p","text":"Particularly useful if moving toward:"},{"type":"h","text":"IT Audit / Technology Risk / IT Controls"}]},{"heading":"Careers You Can Be Hired As","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"After B.Com + relevant skills, possible entry roles include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Audit Associate"},{"text":"Audit Executive"},{"text":"Audit Intern"},{"text":"Accounts Associate"},{"text":"Assurance Associate"},{"text":"Internal Audit Associate"},{"text":"Tax Associate"},{"text":"Finance Associate"},{"text":"Risk & Compliance Associate"},{"text":"Junior Audit Analyst"},{"text":"Audit Analytics Analyst"},{"text":"Accounts Executive"}]},{"type":"p","text":"With experience:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Senior Audit Associate"},{"text":"Audit Senior"},{"text":"Internal Auditor"},{"text":"Tax Senior"},{"text":"Risk Analyst"},{"text":"Assurance Senior"}]},{"type":"h","text":"What Employers May Test"},{"type":"h","text":"Accounting"},{"type":"p","text":"Be comfortable with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Journal entries"},{"text":"Trial balance"},{"text":"Adjustments"},{"text":"Depreciation"},{"text":"Provisions"},{"text":"Revenue"},{"text":"Inventory"},{"text":"Receivables"},{"text":"Payables"},{"text":"Cash flow"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Audit"},{"type":"p","text":"Expect questions about:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Audit risk"},{"text":"Materiality"},{"text":"Audit evidence"},{"text":"Assertions"},{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Vouching"},{"text":"Verification"},{"text":"Internal controls"},{"text":"Substantive testing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Example"},{"type":"p","text":"A company's revenue increased by 40%, but receivables increased by 100%. What would you investigate?"},{"type":"p","text":"A strong candidate should think about:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Revenue recognition","Credit policy","Collection","Ageing","Cut-off","Unusual sales","Customer confirmations"]}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate Study in India","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A PG degree is not mandatory for becoming an Audit Associate."},{"type":"p","text":"Useful options include:"},{"type":"table","header":["PG","Best for"],"rows":[[{"text":"M.Com"},{"text":"Accounting & finance depth"}],[{"text":"MBA Finance"},{"text":"Corporate finance + management"}],[{"text":"MBA Business Analytics"},{"text":"Finance + analytics"}],[{"text":"MSc Finance"},{"text":"Advanced finance"}],[{"text":"PG Diploma in Accounting/Finance"},{"text":"Practical specialisation"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"For professional audit, a relevant professional qualification such as CA/ACCA/CIA can often be more directly aligned than a generic master's."}]},{"heading":"Study Abroad","kind":"abroad","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Potential master's pathways:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MSc Accounting"},{"text":"MSc Accounting & Finance"},{"text":"MSc Audit"},{"text":"MSc Finance"},{"text":"MSc Risk Management"},{"text":"MSc Forensic Accounting"},{"text":"MSc Business Analytics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Potential destinations:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"UK"},{"text":"Ireland"},{"text":"Australia"},{"text":"Canada"},{"text":"USA"},{"text":"Germany"},{"text":"Netherlands"}]},{"type":"p","text":"International students should verify current professional-recognition requirements because accounting and audit qualifications can be jurisdiction-specific."}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"External audit"},{"type":"h","text":"B.Com"},{"type":"h","text":"Audit Intern"},{"type":"h","text":"Audit Associate"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior Audit Associate"},{"type":"h","text":"Audit Manager"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior Manager"},{"type":"h","text":"Director / Partner"},{"type":"h","text":"Internal audit"},{"type":"h","text":"B.Com"},{"type":"h","text":"Internal Audit Associate"},{"type":"h","text":"Internal Auditor"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior Internal Auditor"},{"type":"h","text":"Audit Manager"},{"type":"h","text":"Head of Internal Audit / Chief Audit Executive"},{"type":"h","text":"Professional route"},{"type":"h","text":"B.Com"},{"type":"flow","items":["CA/ACCA pathway","Audit/Assurance","Senior","Manager","Leadership / Practice"]},{"type":"h","text":"Forensic Audit Route"},{"type":"p","text":"Students interested in fraud investigation can add:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Fraud-risk assessment"},{"text":"Transaction analytics"},{"text":"Benford's Law"},{"text":"Data analysis"},{"text":"Evidence documentation"},{"text":"Investigation methodology"},{"text":"Interview techniques"},{"text":"Digital evidence awareness"},{"text":"Excel/SQL/Python"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Possible roles:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Forensic Audit Analyst"},{"text":"Fraud Analyst"},{"text":"Fraud Risk Analyst"},{"text":"Investigation Associate"}]},{"type":"h","text":"IT Audit Route"},{"type":"p","text":"A technology-oriented student can transition toward:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Accounting","Audit","Technology"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"IT general controls"},{"text":"Access controls"},{"text":"Change management"},{"text":"Backup/recovery"},{"text":"Application controls"},{"text":"Cybersecurity fundamentals"},{"text":"IT risk"},{"text":"ERP controls"},{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"Data analytics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Possible progression:"},{"type":"flow","items":["IT Audit Associate","IT Auditor","Senior IT Auditor","IT Audit Manager"]},{"type":"h","text":"2040–2046 Career Evolution"},{"type":"p","text":"Audit is likely to become increasingly data-driven."},{"type":"p","text":"Traditional:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Sample","Test","Document","Report"]},{"type":"p","text":"Future:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Full-population data","Automated testing","AI anomaly detection","Human judgement","Assurance"]},{"type":"p","text":"Important future skills:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Audit analytics"},{"text":"Continuous auditing"},{"text":"AI-assisted audit"},{"text":"Automated controls testing"},{"text":"Process mining"},{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"Python"},{"text":"ERP analytics"},{"text":"Cyber/IT controls"},{"text":"ESG assurance"},{"text":"AI governance"}]},{"type":"p","text":"AI will increasingly automate repetitive testing and documentation, making professional judgement, risk assessment, controls understanding and communication more important."},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended Final Skill Stack"},{"type":"h","text":"Accounting"},{"type":"h","text":"Financial Accounting + Ind AS/IFRS fundamentals"},{"type":"h","text":"Audit"},{"type":"flow","items":["Audit procedures","Assertions","Evidence","Sampling","Risk"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Controls"},{"type":"flow","items":["Internal Controls","Risk Assessment","Control Testing"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Tools"},{"type":"flow","items":["Advanced Excel","Power Query","Accounting/ERP software"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Analytics"},{"type":"flow","items":["SQL","Power BI","Audit Analytics"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Professional"},{"type":"flow","items":["Documentation","Communication","Critical Thinking","Professional Ethics"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Optional specialisation"},{"type":"h","text":"CA / ACCA / CIA / CISA / Forensic Audit"},{"type":"h","text":"Target Progression"},{"type":"h","text":"Year 1"},{"type":"flow","items":["Accounting","Financial Statements","Excel"]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2"},{"type":"flow","items":["Auditing","Assertions","Internal Controls","Advanced Excel"]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3"},{"type":"flow","items":["Audit Procedures","Tax Basics","Accounting Standards","Internship"]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 4"},{"type":"flow","items":["Audit Analytics","Power BI","SQL","Final Audit Project","Placement"]},{"type":"h","text":"Graduation target"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Com Accounting & Finance","strong accounting fundamentals","audit knowledge","Advanced Excel","internal-control understanding","internship","practical audit project."],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Best overall strategy"},{"type":"p","text":"For B.Com – Accounting & Finance → Audit Associate, the strongest route is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Com","Accounting","Auditing","Internal Controls","Advanced Excel","Audit Analytics","Internship","professional qualification pathway where appropriate."],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"The key distinction is to avoid becoming only a “bookkeeping/accounting graduate.” Build toward being an audit professional who can understand financial statements, assess risks and controls, perform evidence-based testing, analyse large datasets and clearly document conclusions."}]}]}